- op: discuss  # f260
  at: '2026-09-17T08:35:40Z'  # f260
  by: agent  # f260
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f260
  clock: 5  # f260
  nonce: f260  # f260
  message: "DONE in PRs #1021 (detector) and #1022 (declarations). Re-ran this row's own\nrepro — find_falsified_dependencies over every survey on disk — after each.\n\nONE OF THE SIX NEEDED NO REPAIR; THE DETECTOR DID. All 68 falsifications of\n`database-query-linker :: [\"sql\"]` emitted NODES and ZERO EDGES. The linker\nmints one query symbol per SQL string it scrapes out of a host file and then\nneeds the sql analyzer's kind=\"table\" symbols for the dst of every edge --\nnodes-with-no-edges is the shape of \"could NOT do its job without the thing it\ndeclared\". The declaration was right; W1's reading was wrong, on 26% of its own\nhits. Two corrections landed in #1021:\n\n  * WHICH OUTPUT FALSIFIES. Was nodes OR edges, on the precedent that keying on\n    edges alone once called a 91-node pass silent. That precedent belongs to\n    SILENCE (\"did this pass say anything?\") and importing it here answered a\n    different question wrong. depends_on is defined as what a linker needs to\n    \"produce its intended edges at all\", and all 59 declarers are linkers (now\n    pinned by a test, so an analyzer declaring depends_on trips the gate rather\n    than going quiet).\n  * WHAT SATISFIES A CLAUSE. Was membership in analysis_runs, which is not a\n    function of the fact it stood in for. Under the WI-jadig / INV-manov\n    file-presence pre-filter an analyzer is short-circuited into skipped_passes\n    only when EVERY language it declares is in the taxonomy's\n    LANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS; all others run and record a 0-file row. On caddy -- a\n    Go repo -- apex/astro/pony are \"active\" and java/ruby/python are not, for\n    the identical fact that the repo has no such files. Production is the same\n    fact under both representations.\n\nRe-measured: 261 (6 clauses / 5 passes) -> 264 of 975 surveys (27.1%, 6 clauses\n/ 4 passes). database-query dropped out; inherited-calls ::\n[\"inheritance-linker\"] became visible at 26; build-target :: [\"toml\",\"json\"]\nwent 4 -> 25.\n\nTHE FIVE REAL ONES SHARE ONE ROOT CAUSE, and it is not five stale lists. Each\nclause was written as \"languages where this concept exists\" -- a statement about\nprogramming languages -- where depends_on means \"passes whose output this pass\nreads\" -- a statement about this tree. Both readings produce a plausible list of\nlanguage names, which is why nothing caught it while nothing read the field.\ninherited-calls-linker is the specimen: the comment above the declaration names\n_MRO_WALKERS as its source of truth and claims to mirror it; INV-fahub's fleet\nPR grew that dict 3 -> 14 and the declaration stayed at three.\n\nREPAIRS (each derived from an enumerated producer set, not re-listed):\n  inherited-calls-linker = Site-1 (enclosing_class INTERSECT _MRO_WALKERS)\n        UNION Site-2 (receiver_type_hint -- needs NO walker, step 1 resolves\n        directly on the inferred type, which is what adds d and kotlin)\n        UNION Site-3 (inherited_field_receiver).\n  inheritance-linker     = the analyzers that write base_classes /\n        included_modules. DROPS rust, dart, elixir -- declared and contributing\n        nothing (rust emits `implements` EDGES, which is type-hierarchy's input,\n        and is declared there). ADDS apex, cpp, go, groovy, objc.\n  type-hierarchy-linker  = the producers of the extends/implements edges it\n        indexes, headed by the pass id inheritance-linker. It never looks at a\n        language, which is exactly why Go repos falsified it.\n  build-target-linker    = the defines_target producers; xml and\n        manifest_targets were missing (Haskell repos falsified [\"toml\",\"json\"]\n        through manifest_targets).\n\nTWO CONJUNCTS DELETED RATHER THAN WIDENED, per this row's \"or rule that a clause\nis deliberately narrow and say why\":\n  inherited-calls :: [\"inheritance-linker\"] -- falsified 26 times and FALSE:\n        Site-2 step 1 emits with no inheritance edges in the graph at all. The\n        ordering it recorded is carried by priority=18 vs inheritance's 15.\n  build-target :: [\"rust\",\"javascript\",\"go\",\"python\",\"java\"] -- it matches a\n        function literally named `main`, which every analyzer emitting functions\n        can supply. The honest enumeration is all 118 and any narrow one is\n        false (yesod falsified it from haskell). A conjunct satisfied by\n        everything states nothing the empty list does not.\n\nGATES so the next registry growth does not re-open this: two AST scans (string\nliterals AND kwarg names count -- a hint key reaches Edge.meta either way;\ncomments do not, which is why AST and not grep) plus a walker-registry gate that\nmaps _MRO_WALKERS through the analyzer registry first. That dict is keyed on\nSymbol.language, a WIDER vocabulary than pass ids -- its `typescript` key has no\npass of its own, so deriving the clause from the keys directly would have\ndeclared a dependency on a nonexistent pass, which validate_pass_name_resolution\nhas no production call site to catch.\n\nFINAL: 264 falsifying surveys -> 0 of 975. Stated as a consistency check, NOT as\nthe argument: widening an OR clause necessarily reduces falsification, and on\ncaddy the repaired clause is satisfied by php as well as by go. The\njustification is per-literal and the gates re-derive it. The zero was confirmed\nlive rather than assumed -- mutate the clause to a language the repo lacks and\nthe detector fires on the same survey.\n\nRESIDUAL FILED SEPARATELY: database-query-linker's SECOND conjunct (11 host\nlanguages) was not falsified and is out of this row's scope, but the linker only\nscans **/*.py, **/*.js, **/*.ts, **/*.java -- so 8 of the 11 literals describe\nneither a pass it reads nor a file it opens. Too wide is the false-all-clear\ndirection."  # f260
